text:
zoe: Weird one - Node sample app showing SSE fragment reassembly issues when auth token rotates quickly. Repro below, but worth noting we only saw this on Node (server side EventSource poly) not browser.

matt: Minimal repro?

zoe: Quick script I ran on my laptop:
```
// reconnect-resume-poc.js
const {EventSource} = require('eventsource');
const url = process.env.URL;
let i = 0;
setInterval(() => {
  const es = new EventSource(url);
  setTimeout(() => es.close(), 110);
  setTimeout(() => {}, 0); // quick spin
  i++;
  if(i>400) process.exit(0);
}, 130);
```
Run with auth-refresh enabled on the server so the token is rotated mid-chunk. After a few hundred loops we get JSON parse errors and sometimes two final tokens.

claire: Logs?

zoe: Trimmed trace: partial payload "{\"choices\": [ { \"text\": \"Hello there\"", then auth refresh triggers reconnect, new conn emits next fragment from another response, then leftover of previous fragment arrives: parser treats them as two separate messages -> duplicated closing bracket and final token.

matt: Sounds like the client parser begins parsing the new connection before the old TCP stream has fully drained; when the old socket emits its tail we end up with interleaved fragments.

claire: Did you try toggling SDK parity flags? We have slightly different reconnect semantics between node/python.

zoe: Yep. Python client with same loop was much more resilient (likely due to its internal buffering). Node shows this most.

matt: Short-term mitigation: server can emit an explicit delimiter / flush event on auth rotation (e.g., "event: reconnect-flush\n\n:\n") to ensure a clean break. Alternatively client-side: hold-until-delimiter mode where the parser will not treat the first chunk from a new connection as complete until a delimiter is observed or a small grace timeout expires.

claire: Another cheap hack: server include a monotonic "x-frag-seq" header per chunk; client drops fragments with seq <= lastSeen when reconnect detected. Safer than doubling final checks.

zoe: I prototyped a client-side seq-drop feature behind flag `drop_stale_fragments_on_reconnect` (default false). Frequency drops to near-zero in my loop.

matt: We should add a lightweight e2e that randomizes auth-refresh timings and reconnect jitter in CI so this doesn't regress.

bot-issue: Created RED-5566: "node sampleapp: SSE resume/fragment interleave on rapid auth rotate" and attached logs + repro script.

ci-bot: Filing test job devex/sse-reconnect-frag-randomized to run nightly and fail if duplicate finals observed.

claire: Long-term: parser should be able to reassemble fragments across reconnects when Last-Event-Id/resume token is present. That requires changing the framing semantics (we'd need server cooperation to include resume tokens).

zoe: I'll open a small PR with the seq-drop flag + repro harness under devex/sampleapp/repro/sse-resume-poc.js and link RED-5566. Assigning @matt and @claire as reviewers. If anyone can run the script locally and sanity-check before I push the CI job that'd be awesome. :thumbsup:
